    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `bulkSignupWarning` flag is a derived, response-only value \u2014 the `Owner` entity has no place to store it, so it must be recomputed at response time from the same repository accumulation the daily-registration rule already counts. Four touch points, each kept small:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (`readOnly`) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `setBulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **New `BulkSignupWarning.java`** \u2014 a tiny cohesive helper (one static method, no surrounding class complexity) that returns `true` when more than 80 owners share the owner's registration date. It mirrors `EnsureDailyRegistrationCapacity`'s counting semantics (comparing `registrationDate`), which the test comment points to (\"shares the same accumulation path exercised by the daily-limit rule\").\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET responder) \u2014 injects `OwnerRepository`, sets the flag on the DTO. This is the path the test exercises (`GET` then assert `bulkSignupWarning == false`).\n\n4. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST responder) \u2014 same one-line addition, so the create response carries the flag too, matching the spec's \"include ... in the response.\"\n\nBoth responders stay at cyclomatic complexity 1 (just a call + setter); all the counting logic lives in the new zero-context helper, keeping structural impact low rather than growing any existing method or class.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the fresh single create returns `bulkSignupWarning: false` as expected.",
